<question type="ddwtos">
  <name><text>VLAN - Port-Typen Access und Trunk konfigurieren</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Die folgende Abbildung zeigt eine VLAN-Konfiguration (Lichtpult = VLAN 10, Dante-Pult = VLAN 20):</p>
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="520" height="220" viewBox="0 0 520 220" style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;display:block;margin:10px auto;"><rect width="520" height="220" rx="8" fill="#f8f9fa" stroke="#dee2e6" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="10" y="17" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#343a40">VLAN-Konfiguration am Switch</text><image href="data:image/svg+xml;base64," x="5" y="25" width="78" height="70"/><text x="44" y="107" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold">Lichtpult</text><text x="44" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#1a6fc4">VLAN 10</text><image href="data:image/svg+xml;base64," x="5" y="135" width="78" height="70"/><text x="44" y="214" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold">Dante-Pult</text><image href="data:image/svg+xml;base64," x="195" y="85" width="66" height="34"/><text x="228" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold">SW-1</text><line x1="83" y1="60" x2="195" y2="96" stroke="#495057" stroke-width="2"/><text x="136" y="65" font-size="10" fill="#1a6fc4" font-weight="bold">Access-Port</text><line x1="83" y1="170" x2="195" y2="109" stroke="#495057" stroke-width="2"/><text x="115" y="152" font-size="10" fill="#2a9d8f" font-weight="bold">Access-Port</text><line x1="261" y1="102" x2="400" y2="102" stroke="#e63946" stroke-width="3"/><text x="330" y="93" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#e63946" font-weight="bold">Trunk-Port</text><rect x="400" y="82" width="110" height="40" rx="5" fill="#dee2e6" stroke="#adb5bd" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="455" y="105" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#495057">Router / SW-2</text></svg>
<p>Ein Endger&#228;t wird an einem <strong>[[1]]</strong>-Port angeschlossen. Verbindungen zwischen zwei Switches nutzen <strong>[[2]]</strong>-Ports. Der IEEE-Standard <strong>[[3]]</strong> definiert das VLAN-Tagging. Pakete ohne VLAN-Tag geh&#246;ren zum <strong>[[4]]</strong> VLAN.</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Access-Port: f&#252;r Endger&#228;te, genau ein VLAN, untagged Traffic. Trunk-Port: verbindet Switches, mehrere VLANs mit IEEE 802.1Q-Tags. Native VLAN: untagged Traffic auf Trunk-Ports (Standard: VLAN 1).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
